    <ix:nonNumeric name="us-gaap:LongLivedAssetsByGeographicAreasTableTextBlock" id="Text_be68f97dd34d4b57ac2b20936a66881f" contextRef="c20250101to20251231" escape="true" continuedAt="Text_6d973b0e47aa49adbf9cfffc4822b0c21"><ix:continuation id="Text_d2e9da6f91cd448585f2d365f72bfffe46" continuedAt="Text_d2e9da6f91cd448585f2d365f72bfffe47">
<div style="text-align: justify; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 10pt;">A major market is defined as a market with long-lived assets greater than 10% of consolidated long-lived assets and also includes the Company&#8217;s country of domicile (the
      United States). Long-lived assets in Mainland China consist primarily of property, plant and equipment related to manufacturing, distribution facilities and the Mainland China headquarters. Long-lived assets in the United States consist primarily of
      property, plant and equipment, including the Company&#8217;s corporate offices and distribution facilities. Long-lived assets by major market are set forth below for the periods ended December 31, 2025, 2024 and 2023:</div>
</ix:continuation></ix:nonNumeric>
